e angle of repose for that material. In your own “lab”, this angle of internal friction can be approximated by the angle of repose: materials placed in a pile to attain a conical shape with slopes (see Figure).","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"uGI9I9zC1h"}],"key":"GoaUWBLZRG"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are many materials can be used to conduct this experiment, such as sugar, salt and flour in your kitchen, or soils, sands, pebbles in your yard. You can also surprise us by being creative!","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"iKzW8QaNfr"}],"key":"NMpIfLSlRK"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Background","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"G2kzOMDOOD"}],"identifier":"background","label":"Background","html_id":"background","implicit":true,"key":"hhdgEEtCkB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"First of all, watch this video for some ideas about what we are going to ask you to do.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"a84zf4n3Q3"}],"key":"yesVQXChUa"},{"type":"iframe","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7UM5R-oMBHc","width":"100%","title":"Angle of Repose Experiments","key":"Ezfq9BvaVT"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"PkKjQwPZBE"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The video below shows the kind of experiment that any of us can try at home - pouring a granular material onto a board and measuring (recording / photographing) the pile as it forms and varying the parameters of the experiment a little to understand what controls the measured values.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"pM7mlciimd"}],"key":"cz361mtg87"},{"type":"iframe","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/SIkRUv39SoI","width":"100%","title":"Angle of Repose Demonstration","key":"QNqsi7giLi"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"fIOXzYSDLW"},{"type":"link","url":"http://www.geotechdata.info/parameter/angle-of-friction","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"website","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"aEiRMvkqas"}],"urlSource":"http://www.geotechdata.info/parameter/angle-of-friction","key":"LeDKajsKTk"},{"type":"text","value":" provides reference values of this angle for some common materials so that it can be used as a benchmark of your experiment. But as mentioned earlier, many other physical conditions such as temperature, humidity, water saturation etc can largely affect this property, thus these reported values can be different from yours by a bit.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"CmUR4omxK2"}],"key":"jRKGB52bFo"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"BLkr33kfht"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that some materials have ","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"AThMF2Sxyh"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cohesion","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"KttDAtsiGM"}],"key":"Nh3G3ic8t0"},{"type":"text","value":" which is what happens when there is still a bond between particles at zero confining pressure. If, for example, you use flour, you would need to sift it to make a pile. Materials that are left lying around will often start to develop cohesion as the particles cement together. If the materials are agitated then they usually can be poured and will “freeze” to a slope with the angle of repose. The video of dry sand avalanching at the beach is an example of this:","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"VBlAjLY4ne"}],"key":"h4eS9LuQdL"},{"type":"iframe","src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/sOOPTZw7FcE","width":"100%","title":"Angle of Repose at the Beach","key":"pqyKo04jx7"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assessment","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"pS46ibG4Wc"}],"identifier":"assessment","label":"Assessment","html_id":"assessment","implicit":true,"key":"TsesJzntYl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Perform a simple set of experiments to demonstrate that granular materials usually pour to form a cone with an angle that is a property of the material itself. You should repeat the experiment for at least two different materials.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"l96yq4BUYX"}],"key":"GpzwBvGW6v"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explain how you photograph / video the material so that you can measure the angle.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"P3o6VwQnbr"}],"key":"Kk4uR0Xzzk"}],"key":"t3fXJh2jfl"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How many times do you need to do this to demonstrate that the angle is the same each time ?  ","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"bBhRlxPkmr"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hint:","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"ehsBchTsYH"}],"key":"TNZFAcjG4P"},{"type":"text","value":" ","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"huUQZuEEUa"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"if you have multiple materials, how many times do you need to do this to show that the angles are actually different ?","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"KVwBT8VhQJ"}],"key":"vYW5IzDYXB"}],"key":"wfPxnk5yz6"}],"key":"ZvIB6UK69U"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify that the angle is approximately independent of factors such as the size of the pile, the speed that the particles land ?","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"LkPpOtMqgU"}],"key":"BFxS9TEvKt"}],"key":"Sn0QA7aH5h"}],"key":"wXpZquzNQa"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a very short experimental report (certainly no more than 2 pages) that introduces the topic,